nty record runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids August to September came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those years. On the middle of the grids, February to March 2025 got 40% of normal and August to September 2025 got 55%. The 2026 numbers so far run the other way, with March to April 2026 at 133% and April to May 2026 at 131% on the middle of the grids.</p>"}
